{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793306581,"nonce":"wfwzRbiARlvZHfRZcWiNtA9A9Y4=","title":"Inline overlay roots lose collected content group ownership and stacking","message":"On bc193006 a green image in a red 50%-opacity overlay_root above a yellow foreground plate renders [255,128,0,255] instead of [128,255,0,255]. The collected image is painted before the foreground, while its root background is painted in the late dynamic owner. Negative: /private/tmp/blinc-overlay-group-negative.log.\n\nCapture supported inline overlay content into its own dynamic visual group, preserving opacity/effects/clips, root ordering and late stacking above ordinary foreground. Overlay roots must remain boundaries for ordinary ancestor groups. Keep unsupported mixed/nested owner combinations and dedicated overlay-tree entry points outside this child until separately verified. Parent e0a7502 retains that scope and release certification.","files":null}]}